{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/925536-allies-and-xp","id":925536,"title":"Allies and XP","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-03T15:42:33-07:00","id":925536,"title":"Allies and XP","content":"So the situation os this: a player of mine asked me to find a police officer, after a while he found one and dominate him to meet him alone and let him drink his blood. With the trigger of dominate 3 he close the vinculum in the successive 2 nights. Now he has a policeman as a trhall without the xp expense for the merit and want to go on with other higher ranks. The question is: is acquires Merits like allies legit even without xp expenditure but just with the roleplayng? If not, how can I manage this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T15:49:40-07:00","id":925537,"title":"","content":"What the XP does for that kind of merits is ensure they have a modicum of plot armor. Sure, you can bribe cops with actual money or blood, but when the elders not to mention, the Hunters, notice some smug neonate trying to one-up them in their own game, things aren't gonna look pretty, not for the cop and not for the character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T16:05:46-07:00","id":925543,"title":"","content":"This is what 2e's Sanctity of Merits refund is for: that's what you get for buying Merits with XP rather than just in-character effort. Your player put in the work: great! They &quot;earned&quot; their thrall, as much as vampires earn anything by the Vinculum. If they don't cash in XP to put him on their sheet, though, the thrall is just like any other non-Merit possession, like a gun or nice clothes at their haven: it's something that can be destroyed by circumstance or even bad luck. Easy come, easy go. Perfectly legit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T16:22:42-07:00","id":925546,"title":"","content":"Another thing you can use as an interim step between &quot;the cop just exists as an NPC,&quot; and &quot;the cop is bought as a Retainer,&quot; is to use Conditions, which can put some mechanical restrictions on how much the cop can do for the PC.<br /> <br /> <br /> One advantage of this is it empowers the player a bit more than ST dictated events that cause the cop to go away; since resolving the Condition (or as a Persistent Condition) can help go towards racking up those Beats to encourage the player to pick a time to &quot;use up&quot; their sway over the cop (even if they don't get the cop killed and decide to go right back to getting the Condition reapplied ASAP), rather than just having a friendly NPC around for &quot;free.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T16:49:19-07:00","id":925559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/925536-allies-and-xp?p=925546#post925546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing you can use as an interim step between &quot;the cop just exists as an NPC,&quot; and &quot;the cop is bought as a Retainer,&quot; is to use Conditions, which can put some mechanical restrictions on how much the cop can do for the PC.<br /> <br /> <br /> One advantage of this is it empowers the player a bit more than ST dictated events that cause the cop to go away; since resolving the Condition (or as a Persistent Condition) can help go towards racking up those Beats to encourage the player to pick a time to &quot;use up&quot; their sway over the cop (even if they don't get the cop killed and decide to go right back to getting the Condition reapplied ASAP), rather than just having a friendly NPC around for &quot;free.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconding this. Conditions, Equipment, and Services are in my opinion a better way to handle these &quot;earned [thing] in roleplay but don't have enough/don't want to spend experience for [Merit]&quot; situations than just giving the Merit free without Sanctity of Merits protecting it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T19:00:28-07:00","id":925628,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I handle this pretty differently. <br /> <br /> The sanctity of merits doesn't provide any plot armor, nor does it make the NPC ally or contact any safer than they'd otherwise be. It just means, as per the book, players can re-spend the lost dots into something else like a replacement ally, or whatever.<br /> <br /> In situations where the player has expressed an interest in doing something like in the OP, I'll either hand out un-sanctified merit dots (freebies which they can't re-spend), allow them to do it but not allow the NPC to factor into the story until they spend the XP to reflect it mechanically, or tell them that the idea doesn't actually occur to the character until they have the XP to spend on it (at which point they can go ahead and do it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","name":"Blitzburger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar231_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T20:25:45-07:00","id":925662,"title":"","content":"What needs to be kept in mind is that XP is an entirely Out of Character resource. Characters don't spend beats or experience points, players do. When someone bloodbonds a member of the police, that serves as justification for buying up Allies or Retainer. All of that happens at the meta-game level, not an in-character perspective. <br /> <br /> So, without the player spending the XP, one really doesn't gain the effects of an Ally or a Retainer. Even if someone is bloodbound, its not a reliable person - the vinculum is easy to resist by simply running away. Its much like the difference between using Resources and Larceny to meet something's Availability - you can steal things every time, but its dangerous and unreliable without the invested Resources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T21:28:02-07:00","id":925692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/925536-allies-and-xp?p=925662#post925662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What needs to be kept in mind is that XP is an entirely Out of Character resource. Characters don't spend beats or experience points, players do. When someone bloodbonds a member of the police, that serves as justification for buying up Allies or Retainer. All of that happens at the meta-game level, not an in-character perspective.<br /> <br /> So, without the player spending the XP, one really doesn't gain the effects of an Ally or a Retainer. Even if someone is bloodbound, its not a reliable person - the vinculum is easy to resist by simply running away. Its much like the difference between using Resources and Larceny to meet something's Availability - you can steal things every time, but its dangerous and unreliable without the invested Resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of the above. In essence, all that the merits really do is facilitate some kind of interaction. The arrangements have been hammered out, the potential risks taken into account and a modus operandi set for the general exchanges.<br /> <br /> Unless that's the focus of a story (and really, it's not a bad one - building power bases is fun, IMO) do portray the steps players are making in order to prevent someone far older, with greater reach and experience from raining on their parade. If it's an improvised thing, all the better to throw monkey-wrenches to add conflict and drama to the stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T02:54:44-07:00","id":925810,"title":"","content":"This is why I'm not entirely sold on making things like allies a merit. It's good in terms of balance, but at the same time, it's very artificial. I am of the opinion that beyond character creation, there's nothing wrong with handing these sorts of merit points. Besides, I like that players actually work towards gaining allies, contacts and money through roleplay rather than just saying &quot;I spend XP to get that&quot;.<br /> <br /> But then again, it really depends on what sort of game you play. Buying merits like these off-screen is probably more suited to a long term political game than a night to night one.<br /> <br /> I don't have a definite answer and in that regard, I'm kind of lucky my players have been very fair with that. They've usually waited until a character was introduced and started interacting with them before asking me to buy an ally or contact merit, so we haven't really had much problems with that. Beyond that, though, there are other characters my players know, either through their backgrounds or through the campaign's events, and these can help them provided the players have been nice to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T03:03:27-07:00","id":925811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Besides, I like that players actually work towards gaining allies, contacts and money through roleplay rather than just saying &quot;I spend XP to get that&quot;. </div> </div> </div> You make it sound like the two are mutually exclusive; rather, they should be mutually inclusive. By all rights, the player shouldn't be able to just &quot;spend XP to get that&quot; without the appropriate roleplay and justifications. I wouldn't allow players to randomly purchase the Allies or Contact (police) merit without the in character actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T07:18:33-07:00","id":925881,"title":"","content":"It's also worth remembering that most such Merits are not &quot;I have a buddy at the precinct,&quot; except maybe the first dot. Allies, Contacts, and Status are supposed to represent sway with large groups of people that you don't get by getting one guy in your pocket. Mentor, Retainer, and True Friend are deep and complex relationships that take time to develop to in being worth of Merits (aka the RP that goes hand-in-hand with the XP as MCN points out); they're not people you walk down the street and pick up because it takes time to find them and cultivate these types of relationships.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T16:37:07-07:00","id":926153,"title":"","content":"I'ad argue that allies can be a single person even at high level. If your ally is the director of the FBI, I'd say that'd qualify as 5 dot, and would mechanically have a similar effect as considering your merit describes a bunch of FBI operatives in different sections.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/925536-allies-and-xp?p=925811#post925811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You make it sound like the two are mutually exclusive; rather, they should be mutually inclusive. By all rights, the player shouldn't be able to just &quot;spend XP to get that&quot; without the appropriate roleplay and justifications. I wouldn't allow players to randomly purchase the Allies or Contact (police) merit without the in character actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the same post, I explain how that's exactly what has happened so far in my current game, so no I'm not saying they are mutually exclusive, I'm just presenting two opposite views and stating which one I like more if I have to choose.<br /> <br /> I still say it can be hard to judge and decide how to handle that stuff. For example, I play in a werewolf game (1ed, but same difference, really where the merits are concerned) where I bought ressource 4 and status 4 at creation (my character's really rich and part of the board of a local TV channel). Later, when I had the XP, I raised both to 5. The most the GM asked me was a manipulation+socialize roll or something to decide how quick I became the CEO and had effective 5 dot status. To be fair, I don't know what he could have asked me to do without it making the game stall, really. Arguably, it was just part of my character's natural trajectory. A bit mor problematic is when I started buying allies dots for an FBI dude. I'm trying to play game, but I'm not actually having a lot of opportunities to justify raising it. It's currently at 3. I basically explained to him my character was looking for a wolf blooded contact in the secret services for later use (the idea being raise the ally to 5, tell him i'm a werewolf and use FBI force as a trump card against the Pure, yeah, I'm playing that Storm Lord like a ventrue). I got far more XP than needed to raise it to 5 (pooled like 60 XP, even though they're 1ed XP), but I don't feel comfortable doing it yet, because I haven't really been able to really do him huge favors ingame. I told the GM I was offering my help as an information channel boss and gathering data about some criminals we know about, but nothing's really come up. At some point, the GM has to throw you a bone too.<br /> <br /> Of course, there's the factor of wether what the player wants to buy is going to derail the GM's story and how much. That's why I think there's no easy answer and it depends on the game. If the GM has a relatively thought up storyline ahead (which is by no means a bad thing), some care is necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T19:19:08-07:00","id":926213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/925536-allies-and-xp?p=926153#post926153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'ad argue that allies can be a single person even at high level. If your ally is the director of the FBI, I'd say that'd qualify as 5 dot, and would mechanically have a similar effect as considering your merit describes a bunch of FBI operatives in different sections.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you can run it that way if you want - golden rule and all - but that's not how the Merit is actually phrased. It's called &quot;Allies&quot; not &quot;Ally.&quot; It gets you influence in a group, not influence with a person who then uses their own advantages on your behalf (which is a Retainer). <br /> <br /> The FBI director doesn't handle most things. Hell, most of the 35,000+ employees of the FBI have probably never met one of the directors - at best they might have been at an event with the director and shook a hand - leaving most of them having no idea who the hell you are and why they should do anything for you. And the FBI director isn't going to call up a field office to tell them to give a friend access to the crime lab for their own personal investigations; because that's pretty much a guarantee that they'll get fired for corruption.<br /> <br /> That's why Allies is about groups. Having influence with a group explains why you can get favors from their whole organization. Members/employees/etc. know who you are, and why people do you favors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the same post, I explain how that's exactly what has happened so far in my current game, so no I'm not saying they are mutually exclusive, I'm just presenting two opposite views and stating which one I like more if I have to choose. </div> </div> </div>Phrasing it as &quot;two opposite views,&quot; is basically saying they are mutually exclusive by making them a binary issue. Sure, 1e had holes in it that made it harder to judge. That's why 2e added the Sanctity of Merits rules, and has Conditions/Equipment that can overlap with Merits in concept (the Connected Condition is pretty much exactly for the OP's issue of working for influence in a group but not yet having the XP to buy Allies, and there's Cash Equipment for when you find a pile of money instead of having to buy up Resources).<br /> <br /> You don't have to worry about giving way free Merit dots, because Merits aren't meant to be free like that. You have other things to act as an interim between in-character actions and putting XP into the effort (if you ever do, since you can just work Conditions if you want); players have a reason to invest time in the RP justification for Merits. It can even help with the ST's pacing/plot because, again, there's a middle point you can use so players can feel like they're getting stuff for their efforts, even if the ST doesn't want them to get to the point of investing XP on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T03:40:29-07:00","id":926350,"title":"","content":"Well, that's one way to see things. I don't agree that 2ed fixes whatever holes 1ed had. It brings different solutions, but I wouldn't say either is objectively better. That said, I believe sanctity of merit is a good way of helping the players not feel ripped off while allowing the GM to fuck with them anyway. I still say the exact way of handling merit depends on what kind of game you wanna play. I still see an argument for buying merits and not worry about the details just as I see the point in handling merits for free and not bother with the XP cost (and obviously, anything in between).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/925536-allies-and-xp?p=926213#post926213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Phrasing it as &quot;two opposite views,&quot; is basically saying they are mutually exclusive by making them a binary issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, two opposite views are &quot;buying merits with XP only&quot; and &quot;getting merits via roleplay only&quot;. Let me rephrase that, these are two extremes of the spectrum. Now, how about we don't split hair over how we word things ? You know exactly what I was saying, so let's not start arguing about something so pointless, please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T08:32:48-07:00","id":926434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/925536-allies-and-xp?p=926350#post926350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that's one way to see things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes... and it's the way the book says things are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't agree that 2ed fixes whatever holes 1ed had. It brings different solutions, but I wouldn't say either is objectively better. </div> </div> </div>You're treating house rules to 1e (things like giving away Merits for free, giving purchased Merits &quot;plot armor&quot; so players wouldn't lose XP for losing Merits, allowing people to buy Merits with XP debt, buying Merits with XP only, etc) as actual rules in 1e. They weren't. RAW, in 1e, if you don't spend XP on a Merit, you don't have it. There's no, &quot;give it away for RP&quot; clause in the Merits section.<br /> <br /> 2e definitely fixed this by having Conditions that can serve as interim mechanics without having to either give the Merits before XP is spent (free or through XP debt), or Equipment/Services.<br /> <br /> While many things are subjective regarding games, 2e having official solutions, while 1e had no official solution is as close to an objective improvement as possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, two opposite views are &quot;buying merits with XP only&quot; and &quot;getting merits via roleplay only&quot;. Let me rephrase that, these are two extremes of the spectrum. </div> </div> </div>Both of these positions are still misleading for what the text describes. They're not opposite views, they're not a spectrum. RAW they're two pieces to adding dots to your sheet: RP why, spend XP. How much RP a group likes before considering a purchase justified is subjective and depends on the group/the mode of play at the time. Having to spend XP to get Merits is the RAW that doesn't change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You know exactly what I was saying, so let's not start arguing about something so pointless, please. </div> </div> </div>No, I didn't. This is a purely text based medium where we only have each other's words to go on. If it isn't directly stated, you shouldn't expect people to gather the correct inferences you intend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T11:55:14-07:00","id":928844,"title":"","content":"One must also remember that these merits generally aren't just &quot;you have a friend.&quot; They give mechanical advantages. Blocking social merits, getting information.<br /> <br /> What I do is require players to pay for the merit if they want those mechanical advantages. Otherwise, they just treat the friend as any other NPC with a favorable opinion of the PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T05:02:16-07:00","id":929197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/925536-allies-and-xp?p=928844#post928844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One must also remember that these merits generally aren't just &quot;you have a friend.&quot; They give mechanical advantages. Blocking social merits, getting information.<br /> <br /> What I do is require players to pay for the merit if they want those mechanical advantages. Otherwise, they just treat the friend as any other NPC with a favorable opinion of the PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is also what I do.<br /> <br /> Requiring the Allies merit to have any NPCs the players can consider 'allies' is silly. Requiring it to gain the mechanical benefit of 'Allies' is not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T12:28:21-07:00","id":929327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/925536-allies-and-xp?p=928844#post928844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One must also remember that these merits generally aren't just &quot;you have a friend.&quot; They give mechanical advantages. Blocking social merits, getting information.<br /> <br /> What I do is require players to pay for the merit if they want those mechanical advantages. Otherwise, they just treat the friend as any other NPC with a favorable opinion of the PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Also something quite similar to what I do with my group. <br /> <br /> They might have an ally in the PD that helps out because the RP lead to the NPC becoming a friend... but I dont give the mechanical advantages or safe guard that cop in any way until the PCs buy the dot with exp. Most recently I had that &quot;ally&quot; NPC in the Police department get suspended because the players kept drawing on her again and again with no dots to support her mechanically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}